Chapter: LirNullaryCross
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The shapes that lower to a LIR function with NO instructions: a single
 block whose result is a parameter or an immediate. `ident` lowers to
 `b0: => v0`, `konst` to `b0: => #42`, `pick2` to `b0: => v1`.

 This is the first construct the ARM64 LIR selector claims
 (`codex/plugs/arm64/Arm64Lir.codex`), so on that backend these
 definitions are emitted by a different code path from every other
 function in the file. x86-64 compiles them the way it always did, which
 is what makes the two answers comparable.

 `pick-last` and `pick-mid` are here because the interesting case is a
 result that is NOT parameter zero: parameter `i` arrives in `x_i`, so a
 selector that ignored the index and returned whatever was in `x0` would
 pass `ident` and fail these. `deep` pushes that to the eighth argument,
 the last one the ABI passes in a register.

 `via-call` exists so the answers are not read only from the definitions
 themselves: it calls them, which means the function offsets and arities
 the selector registers have to be right for an ordinary call to land.

Section: Nullary and Projection

  ident : Integer -> Integer
  ident (x) = x

  konst : Integer
  konst = 42

  neg-konst : Integer
  neg-konst = 0 - 7

  big-konst : Integer
  big-konst = 123456789

  pick2 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pick2 (a) (b) = b

  pick-mid : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pick-mid (a) (b) (c) = b

  pick-last : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  pick-last (a) (b) (c) = c

  deep : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  deep (a) (b) (c) (d) (e) (f) (g) (h) = h

  via-call : Integer -> Integer
  via-call (n) = ident n + pick2 n 5

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("ident: " & show (ident 7))
    print-line-uni ("konst: " & show konst)
    print-line-uni ("neg-konst: " & show neg-konst)
    print-line-uni ("big-konst: " & show big-konst)
    print-line-uni ("pick2: " & show (pick2 3 9))
    print-line-uni ("pick-mid: " & show (pick-mid 1 2 3))
    print-line-uni ("pick-last: " & show (pick-last 1 2 3))
    print-line-uni ("deep: " & show (deep 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8))
    print-line-uni ("via-call: " & show (via-call 10))
  end
